{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"skaldic-carbon-copperhead","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nA batch of 46 concurrent `search` calls was canceled at the client. A subsequent single `search` remained unserved and failed with `timed out awaiting tools/call after 300s`. The canceled calls were read-only.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Canceled or abandoned searches cannot monopolize MCP request capacity.\n- [ ] A later single tracker read completes within the normal request budget.\n- [ ] A regression test covers cancellation/backpressure for concurrent searches.","id":"b0c3-7455-86df-48f6","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["mcp","concurrency","reliability"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Canceled MCP searches starve later tracker reads"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788557999468311001,"uuid":"a94e8287-fc69-44cc-862a-82020cfa4b21"}